# AI Executive Assistant — environment configuration
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in real credentials. Never commit `.env`.

# --- Google (Gmail, Calendar, Drive) ---------------------------------------
# Gmail, Calendar and Drive share ONE Google account / OAuth consent.
# You log in once with `python -m ai_assistant.integrations.google_auth`,
# which stores a refresh token to GOOGLE_TOKEN_FILE and then refreshes the
# short-lived access token automatically on every run.
#
# Provide installed-app ("desktop") OAuth client credentials either inline
# via GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID + GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, or point GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_FILE
# at a client_secret*.json downloaded from the Google Cloud console.
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
# GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS_FILE=./client_secret.json
#
# Where the authorized-user token (including the refresh token) is stored.
# Defaults to .google_token.json (git-ignored). Uncomment to override.
# GOOGLE_TOKEN_FILE=.google_token.json
#
# CLOUD PATH (GitHub Actions): a runner has no token file, so supply the SAME
# refresh token through the environment instead. After the one-time local login
# above, read the value out of your GOOGLE_TOKEN_FILE ("refresh_token" field)
# and store it as a repository secret together with the client id/secret:
#   GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID, GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET, GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN
# Precedence: token file (if present) -> GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN -> skipped.
# GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN=
#
# SCOPES / RE-CONSENT (read this if a meeting-note summary says it cannot open
# the document). The requested scopes are gmail.readonly, calendar.readonly,
# drive.metadata.readonly AND drive.readonly. The last one is what allows
# READING a document's content (files.export / files.get_media); metadata alone
# only allows LISTING. Scopes are frozen into the refresh token at consent
# time, so a token issued before drive.readonly was added KEEPS THE OLD SCOPES
# and every content read fails with a 403. To pick up the new scope:
#   1. delete GOOGLE_TOKEN_FILE (default .google_token.json)
#   2. run `python -m ai_assistant.integrations.google_auth` again
#   3. copy the NEW refresh token into GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN (and the GitHub
#      secret of the same name)
# Nothing breaks until you do: listing keeps working and content reads degrade
# to a message that names this exact problem.

# ============================================
# Google OAuth 2.0 - Gmail & Calendar
# ============================================
# Get from Google Cloud Console:
# https://console.cloud.google.com/

GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=your-client-id-here.apps.googleusercontent.com
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=your-client-secret-here

# Refresh token (auto-generated during setup)
# Run: python -m src.ai_assistant.integrations.google_oauth_setup
GOOGLE_OAUTH_REFRESH_TOKEN=

# OAuth callback URL (local development)
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CALLBACK_URL=http://localhost:8080/oauth/callback

# Gmail Agent Configuration
MAIL_ANALYST_ENABLED=true
MAIL_ANALYST_MAX_EMAILS=50
MAIL_ANALYST_LOOKBACK_HOURS=24

# Day Planner Agent Configuration
DAY_PLANNER_ENABLED=true
DAY_PLANNER_TIMEZONE=Europe/Istanbul
DAY_PLANNER_WORKDAY_START=09:00
DAY_PLANNER_WORKDAY_END=18:00
DAY_PLANNER_LOOKAHEAD_DAYS=7

# --- Slack ------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# THE RECOMMENDED WAY TO FILL IN EVERY SLACK_CHANNEL_* BELOW:
#
#     python -m ai_assistant.integrations.slack_setup             # dry run
#     python -m ai_assistant.integrations.slack_setup --apply     # create them
#     python -m ai_assistant.integrations.slack_setup --apply --write-env
#
# That script creates one main channel plus one channel per advisor, sets each
# channel's Turkish purpose and topic, invites the bot, and prints (or writes)
# the ids in exactly the form below. It is idempotent — re-run it after adding
# an advisor and it only creates what is missing.
#
# Bot User OAuth Token from your Slack app (starts with "xoxb-").
# REQUIRED for one-channel-per-advisor delivery: only chat.postMessage can
# choose a channel. Scopes: chat:write, channels:read, channels:manage,
# channels:join (+ groups:read, groups:write for the private channels).
SLACK_BOT_TOKEN=
# Incoming Webhook URL — the simplest single-channel setup.
# CAUTION: a webhook is bound to ONE channel at creation time and Slack IGNORES
# the channel field in the payload. With only a webhook the daily summary is
# still delivered, but the per-advisor fan-out is skipped (it would silently
# dump every advisor into the same room). Use a bot token for sub-channels.
SLACK_WEBHOOK_URL=
# Legacy single-channel setting; kept as the last fallback. Channel id or name.
SLACK_CHANNEL=
# THE MAIN CHANNEL. It carries the SUMMARY: one line per advisor with its
# headline, a link to the full report on the dashboard, and a link into that
# advisor's own channel. Takes priority over SLACK_CHANNEL.
SLACK_MAIN_CHANNEL=

# --- One sub-channel per advisor ---------------------------------------------
# Each advisor's own section goes to its own channel, in full. Format:
# SLACK_CHANNEL_<ADVISOR_KEY>, where <ADVISOR_KEY> is the advisor's stable
# identifier in UPPERCASE with underscores.
#
# An advisor with no channel here falls back to SLACK_MAIN_CHANNEL (then
# SLACK_CHANNEL). Leaving ALL of them empty is a valid, supported setup: the
# fan-out then stays off entirely and only the summary is delivered, exactly
# as before this feature existed.
#
# The thirteen advisors, their keys and the channel slack_setup creates for each:
#   Sabah İşletme Brifingi       SLACK_CHANNEL_MORNING_OPERATIONS      #ai-sabah-operasyon
#   İletişim & Takvim Danışmanı  SLACK_CHANNEL_COMMUNICATIONS_CALENDAR #ai-iletisim-takvim 🔒
#   Toplantı Hazırlık & Takip    SLACK_CHANNEL_MEETING_PREP            #ai-toplanti-hazirlik 🔒
#   Kariyer Gelişimi             SLACK_CHANNEL_CAREER_DEVELOPMENT      #ai-kariyer-gelisim
#   Pazar İstihbaratı            SLACK_CHANNEL_MARKET_INTELLIGENCE     #ai-pazar-istihbarat
#   Müşteri Şikayet & İtibar     SLACK_CHANNEL_COMPLAINT_RADAR         #ai-sikayet-radari
#   Veri Analisti                SLACK_CHANNEL_DATA_ANALYST            #ai-veri-analisti 🔒
#   Yapay Zeka & İnovasyon       SLACK_CHANNEL_AI_INNOVATION           #ai-yapayzeka-inovasyon 🔒
#   Çocuk Gelişimi Danışmanı     SLACK_CHANNEL_KIDS_DEVELOPMENT        #ai-cocuk-gelisim
#   Yönetici Koçu                SLACK_CHANNEL_EXECUTIVE_COACHING      #ai-yonetici-koclugu 🔒
#   İş Analisti Danışmanı        SLACK_CHANNEL_WORK_ANALYST            #ai-is-analisti 🔒
#   Operasyon Direktörü          SLACK_CHANNEL_OPERATIONS_DIRECTOR     #ai-operasyon-direktoru 🔒
#   Teknik Gözetim (7/24 SRE)    SLACK_CHANNEL_SRE_WATCHDOG            #ai-teknik-gozetim 🔒
#
# 🔒 = handles personal data (or the system's own internals); never published to
#      the public dashboard, so its body lives ONLY in that Slack channel.
#      slack_setup creates these eight as PRIVATE channels by default (pass
#      --all-public to opt out).
#
# Example (uncomment to use, or let --write-env fill them in):
# SLACK_CHANNEL_MORNING_OPERATIONS=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_COMMUNICATIONS_CALENDAR=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_MEETING_PREP=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_CAREER_DEVELOPMENT=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_MARKET_INTELLIGENCE=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_COMPLAINT_RADAR=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_DATA_ANALYST=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_AI_INNOVATION=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_KIDS_DEVELOPMENT=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_EXECUTIVE_COACHING=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_WORK_ANALYST=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_OPERATIONS_DIRECTOR=C0123456789
# SLACK_CHANNEL_SRE_WATCHDOG=C0123456789

# --- Todoist ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal API token from Todoist > Settings > Integrations > Developer.
TODOIST_API_TOKEN=

# --- Notion -----------------------------------------------------------------
# Internal integration secret from https://www.notion.so/my-integrations
# (starts with "secret_" or "ntn_").
NOTION_API_KEY=

# --- Asana ------------------------------------------------------------------
# Personal access token from Asana account settings > Apps and integrations > Personal access tokens.
# Generate a token with task and project scopes.
ASANA_TOKEN=
# Workspace ID where projects will be created (find it in Asana URL: app.asana.com/0/<workspace_id>).
ASANA_WORKSPACE_ID=
# Optional project name template for created projects. Each advisor can have its own project.
# Default template: "{advisor_name}_project" (e.g., "Yapay Zeka Haberleri_project").
# ASANA_PROJECT_TEMPLATE={advisor_name}_project

# --- LLM provider (choose one) ----------------------------------------------
# Google Gemini API key (preferred if both are set).
GEMINI_API_KEY=
# OpenAI API key (used if GEMINI_API_KEY is empty).
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Gemini generation model (default: gemini-2.5-flash). Must be valid on the
# v1beta generateContent endpoint (e.g. gemini-2.5-flash, gemini-2.0-flash).
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash
# Model fallback chain (comma-separated). If the primary model keeps answering
# 503 "model overloaded" (or is unavailable), these are tried in order.
# Leave blank to keep the built-in chain.
# GEMINI_FALLBACK_MODELS=gemini-flash-latest,gemini-2.0-flash
# Max output tokens for generation (default: 8192). gemini-2.5-flash is a
# "thinking" model; a low budget truncates the visible answer, so keep it
# generous enough for the deep, multi-section briefings.
# GEMINI_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=8192
# Per-request timeout in seconds (default: 120) so a hung call can never stall
# the daily job. Raise it if you also raise the token budget.
# GEMINI_TIMEOUT_SECONDS=120
# Free-tier resilience — the free Gemini quota returns HTTP 429 after a couple
# of rapid calls, and the service itself occasionally returns 5xx. The client
# retries 429 AND 500/502/503/504 with backoff (honouring Retry-After), then
# falls back to the next model in the chain.
# GEMINI_MAX_RETRIES: how many times to retry a transient failure (default: 4).
# GEMINI_MAX_RETRIES=4
# GEMINI_RETRY_BASE_SECONDS: base backoff in seconds; grows 20s, 40s, 60s, 60s
# by default (capped at 3x the base).
# GEMINI_RETRY_BASE_SECONDS=20
# GEMINI_REQUEST_SPACING_SECONDS: optional pause before each Gemini call to
# spread sequential advisor calls across quota windows (default: 0 = off).
# GEMINI_REQUEST_SPACING_SECONDS=0

# --- Batched digest (free-tier quota saver) ---------------------------------
# The free Gemini tier allows only a couple of generateContent calls per quota
# window, so by default the WHOLE advisor team is served by ONE batched call
# instead of one call per advisor. Set to "false" to go back to per-advisor
# calls (useful for debugging a single section).
# DIGEST_BATCH_MODE=true
# Token budget for that single batched answer — it carries every section, so it
# needs far more headroom than one briefing (default: 32768).
# DIGEST_BATCH_MAX_OUTPUT_TOKENS=32768

# --- Weather advisor (RETIRED from the live roster) --------------------------
# The weather advisor no longer runs; the module is kept on disk so putting it
# back is a one-line change in ai_assistant.advisors.all_advisors(). These
# settings are inert until then.
# City to geocode for the daily weather briefing. Leave empty to use the
# built-in default "Istanbul"; any value here (or a GitHub secret) overrides it.
WEATHER_CITY=
# Optional country name/code to disambiguate the city (e.g. "Turkey" / "TR").
WEATHER_COUNTRY=
# Alternatively, provide explicit coordinates (these override WEATHER_CITY).
# WEATHER_LATITUDE=41.0082
# WEATHER_LONGITUDE=28.9784

# --- Job scout advisor (İş Avcısı) — LLM-backed -----------------------------
# Role keywords to prepare applications and build search links for. Leave empty
# to use the built-in default ("çağrı merkezi müdürü, müşteri deneyimi
# yöneticisi, operasyon müdürü"); a value here overrides it.
# NOTE: the advisor only PREPARES material + plain search URLs; it never logs
# in or auto-submits applications to LinkedIn/Kariyer.net.
JOB_KEYWORDS=
# Location hint used in the search links. Default: "İstanbul".
JOB_LOCATION=

# --- Sector / certs advisors (Sektör İstihbaratı & Sertifika) ---------------
# Your sector/field; tailors sector intel + free-cert suggestions.
# Default if empty: "banka çağrı merkezleri".
USER_SECTOR=
# RSS/Atom feed of sector news folded into the sector briefing. Default if
# empty: a Turkish Google News search feed for "çağrı merkezi banka", so the
# briefing can cite real, verifiable links out of the box.
SECTOR_NEWS_RSS_URL=

# --- AI news advisor (Yapay Zeka Haberleri) ---------------------------------
# RSS/Atom feed of AI news; the latest items are summarized. Default if empty:
# a Turkish Google News search feed for "yapay zeka". If the feed is
# unreachable, the advisor degrades to an LLM roundup (with a caveat).
AI_NEWS_RSS_URL=

# --- Banka & Çağrı Merkezi Proje Uzmanı (deep domain expert) ----------------
# Outsourcing governance + information security + compliance for bank contact
# centers, with a rotating daily deep-dive focus.
# RSS/Atom feed of Turkish banking / contact-center / outsourcing news, folded
# into the briefing so it can cite REAL, verifiable links. Default if empty: a
# Turkish Google News search feed. An unreachable feed degrades to LLM-only.
# NOTE: this advisor deliberately describes regulatory PRINCIPLES and names real
# frameworks (BDDK support-service & information-systems regulations, KVKK,
# ISO/IEC 27001, PCI-DSS, SOC 2) instead of citing article numbers or dates, and
# always appends a "confirm with your compliance/legal team" caveat.
BANKING_NEWS_RSS_URL=
# Second, optional feed for the same advisor, weighted towards regulation, data
# protection and information-security news. Default if empty: a Turkish Google
# News search feed for KVKK / bilgi güvenliği / veri ihlali in banking. Items
# from both feeds are merged and de-duplicated.
BANKING_SECURITY_RSS_URL=

# --- Yapay Zeka Ustalığı Koçu (AI mastery coach) ----------------------------
# Skill track the coach teaches at: temel | orta | ileri.
# Default if empty: temel.
AI_MASTERY_LEVEL=
# RSS/Atom feed of free AI training / certificate announcements, used to ground
# the "ücretsiz sertifikalı eğitimler" block in REAL links. Default if empty: a
# Turkish Google News search feed for ücretsiz yapay zeka eğitimi/sertifika.
AI_MASTERY_RSS_URL=

# --- Çağrı Merkezi & Müşteri Deneyimi Araştırmacısı (CX research) -----------
# RSS/Atom feed of customer-experience / contact-center news. Real items are
# always preferred over recalled statistics. Default if empty: a Turkish Google
# News search feed for müşteri deneyimi / çağrı merkezi / müşteri memnuniyeti.
CX_RESEARCH_RSS_URL=

# --- Müşteri Şikayet & İtibar Radarı (complaint radar) ----------------------
# Bankalar ve finans kurumları hakkındaki müşteri şikâyet gündemini okur:
# temalara göre gruplar, kurumların çözüm yaklaşımını yorumlar, hacim değişimini
# ve rakip kıyasını çıkarır.
# HİÇBİRİNİN VARSAYILANI YOKTUR — bu bölüm bilerek opt-in'dir. Hiç besleme
# tanımlı değilse danışman Türkçe bir açıklamayla `skipped` olur ve koşuyu
# düşürmez.
# Ana şikâyet / itibar RSS-Atom akışı (örn. bir şikâyet platformunun ya da bir
# Google Haberler aramasının besleme adresi).
COMPLAINT_RADAR_RSS_URL=
# İkinci, isteğe bağlı akış: sektör geneli / finans kurumları şikâyet ve itibar
# haberleri. İki akış TEK havuzda birleştirilir ve başlığa göre tekilleştirilir.
COMPLAINT_RADAR_SECTOR_RSS_URL=
# Takip edilen KENDİ markalarınız, virgülle ayrılmış (örn. "Banka A, Banka A
# Mobil"). Boşsa radar akıştaki bütün kurumlara bakar.
COMPLAINT_RADAR_BRANDS=
# Kıyaslanacak rakipler, virgülle ayrılmış. Boşsa rakip kıyası yalnızca akışta
# ADI GEÇEN kurumlarla yapılır; kurum adı asla uydurulmaz.
COMPLAINT_RADAR_COMPETITORS=

# --- Ücretsiz Sertifika & Eğitim Araştırmacısı ------------------------------
# Feed of free-course / certificate announcements, so the suggestions can cite
# current, REAL announcements. Default if empty: a Turkish Google News search.
FREE_CERTS_RSS_URL=

# --- Veri Analisti (data analyst, analysis engine) ---------------------------
# The data analyst reads the operation's OWN spreadsheet through the analysis
# engine (ai_assistant.analysis) and interprets it: why a metric moved, what it
# costs operationally, what to do about it. With NEITHER of the two variables
# below set, the advisor is `skipped` with a Turkish note explaining this block.
#
# 1) An explicit source — a local Excel/CSV path, a Google Sheets link or a
#    sheet id. A Sheets link needs the spreadsheets.readonly OAuth scope.
DATA_ANALYST_SOURCE=
# 2) …or a Drive folder to watch: the MOST RECENTLY MODIFIED spreadsheet in it
#    is picked automatically, so "drop today's export in the folder" just works.
DATA_ANALYST_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID=
# Optional: which sheet/tab to read (default: the first visible one).
DATA_ANALYST_SHEET=
# Optional: analyse only the last N days of the date column.
DATA_ANALYST_LAST_DAYS=
# Optional: service-level target the SLA finding is judged against (default 80).
DATA_ANALYST_SLA_TARGET=
# Optional: rows kept per breakdown table (default 25).
DATA_ANALYST_TOP_N=
# Optional: a specific question to answer from today's data, in Turkish.
DATA_ANALYST_QUESTION=

# --- Operasyon Direktörü (operations director) -------------------------------
# Runs LAST, after every other advisor including the work analyst, and turns the
# whole run into a prioritised decision list — each item with an owner, a
# deadline and the consequence of not acting. It owns the BUSINESS operation
# (staffing, SLA risk, backlog, escalation); the SYSTEM's technical health stays
# with the work analyst and is deliberately kept out of this section.
#
# Needs no source of its own: it synthesises the other advisors' output. With
# nothing to synthesise it is `skipped`, never a traceback.
# Optional: what the operation IS, used to frame the decisions.
OPERATIONS_DIRECTOR_BUSINESS=
# Optional: expected volume / forecast for the coming days, free text
# (e.g. "hafta içi ~1.200 çağrı/gün, cuma %20 yüksek").
OPERATIONS_DIRECTOR_FORECAST=
# Optional: the SLA commitment the risk assessment is measured against
# (e.g. "%80 çağrı 20 sn içinde").
OPERATIONS_DIRECTOR_SLA_TARGET=

# --- Findings memory (deduplication across runs) ----------------------------
# The team runs several times a day (see BRIEFING_MODE below) and must not
# repeat itself, so every DELIVERED finding is fingerprinted into a small JSON
# ledger. Only hashes are stored — never the briefing text.
# Default if empty: .assistant_state/findings.json. Like the accountability
# state, the Daily Briefing workflow commits this file back to `main` after each
# run, which is what makes the memory survive the ephemeral runner. Leave unset
# in CI so the committed default path is used.
FINDINGS_MEMORY_FILE=
# Rolling retention window in days: an entry older than this is forgotten, so a
# genuinely recurring-but-stale topic may resurface. Default if empty: 30.
FINDINGS_MEMORY_DAYS=

# --- Run mode (one full briefing + incremental top-ups) ---------------------
# full        -> the complete daily briefing (all advisors, all sections).
#                This is the default and what the 10:00 İstanbul run uses.
# incremental -> report ONLY findings that are new since the last run; advisors
#                with nothing new collapse to "yeni bulgu yok", no model call is
#                made when nobody has anything, and Slack is skipped entirely on
#                a completely quiet run. Used by the 14:00/18:00/22:00 runs.
# BRIEFING_MODE=full
# Whether a quiet incremental run stays out of Slack (default: true). The full
# daily briefing ALWAYS sends, whatever this is set to.
# SKIP_SLACK_WHEN_NOTHING_NEW=true

# --- Hesap Sorucu Koç (accountability coach) --------------------------------
# Small JSON file holding each day's assigned tasks + the streak counter.
# Default if empty: .assistant_state/accountability.json.
# On GitHub Actions the runner filesystem is EPHEMERAL, so the Daily Briefing
# workflow COMMITS this file back to `main` after every run — that is what makes
# the streak durable. Leave this unset in CI so the committed default path is
# used; overriding it there silently disables the persistence. A missing file is
# still a clean fresh start. This advisor makes NO LLM call.
ACCOUNTABILITY_STATE_FILE=

# --- Gün Başı Operasyon Brifingi (Gmail + Calendar) -------------------------
# Uses the SHARED Google OAuth above (read-only scopes) — no extra credentials.
# Until you run `python -m ai_assistant.integrations.google_auth` once, this
# advisor reports `skipped`, which is the expected state. To run it in GitHub
# Actions, set the GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID / GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET / GOOGLE_REFRESH_TOKEN
# secrets described in the Google section above.
# How many recent messages to look at (default: 12, hard-capped at 25).
# OPS_BRIEFING_MAX_EMAILS=12
# Gmail "newer_than" window; <n>h or <n>d only (default: 1d).
# OPS_BRIEFING_EMAIL_WINDOW=1d

# --- Toplantı Hazırlık & Takip (meeting prep) -------------------------------
# Yaklaşan toplantıyı Google Takvim'den, geçmiş toplantı notlarını Google
# Drive'dan okur ve toplantı öncesi hazırlık notu yazar. Yukarıdaki PAYLAŞILAN
# Google OAuth'u kullanır — ayrı kimlik YOKTUR. Kimlik yoksa ya da yaklaşan
# toplantı bulunamazsa Türkçe bir açıklamayla `skipped` olur.
# Kaç gün ilerisine bakılacağı (varsayılan: 3).
# MEETING_PREP_LOOKAHEAD_DAYS=3
# Toplantı notlarının durduğu Drive klasörünün id'si. Boşsa yukarıdaki
# GOOGLE_DRIVE_FOLDER_ID kullanılır; o da boşsa not eşleme atlanır ve hazırlık
# notu yalnızca takvim kaydından yazılır.
MEETING_PREP_NOTES_FOLDER_ID=
# Bir toplantıya en fazla kaç geçmiş not eşlenir (varsayılan: 3).
# MEETING_PREP_MAX_NOTES=3
# NOT: not İÇERİĞİNİ okumak drive.readonly kapsamını gerektirir. Kapsam listesi
# artık onu istiyor, ama ESKİ bir refresh token yeni kapsamı kendiliğinden
# almaz (yukarıdaki "SCOPES / RE-CONSENT" bölümüne bakın): yeniden onay
# verilene kadar not başlık + tarih düzeyinde kullanılır, bölüm yine üretilir.

# --- Anka bridge (Anka Köprüsü) — RETIRED from the live roster ---------------
# The bridge no longer runs; the module is kept on disk so putting it back is a
# one-line change in ai_assistant.advisors.all_advisors(). These settings are
# inert until then.
# Endpoint for your external "Anka" assistant. This one has NO default — the
# URL is specific to you, so without it the bridge stays `skipped` by design.
# ANKA_API_URL is accepted as an alias for ANKA_WEBHOOK_URL.
ANKA_WEBHOOK_URL=
# ANKA_API_URL=
# Optional bearer token sent as "Authorization: Bearer <key>".
ANKA_API_KEY=
# Optional HTTP method for the trigger request (default: POST).
# ANKA_HTTP_METHOD=POST

# --- Optional tuning --------------------------------------------------------
# Timeout in seconds for each outbound health-check request (default: 10).
AI_ASSISTANT_HTTP_TIMEOUT=10

# --- Ajan panosu (live dashboard) -------------------------------------------
# Where the machine-readable run status is written after every briefing (the
# file the static dashboard in frontend/ renders). Default if empty:
# frontend/status.json — which is also the path the Daily Briefing workflow
# commits back to `main`, so leave this unset in CI. The file NEVER contains
# briefing content or API keys: only statuses, sanitised reasons and character
# counts. A failure to write it is logged and ignored; it can never break the
# briefing.
STATUS_REPORT_FILE=

# --- Rapor belgeleri (per-advisor reading pages) -----------------------------
# Every advisor's section is written as its OWN document under
# frontend/reports/<YYYY-MM-DD>/<ajan>.json, and the dashboard renders those as
# mobile-first reading pages. Slack no longer carries the briefing itself — it
# carries one line per advisor plus a link into this directory.
#
# Where those documents are written. Default if empty: frontend/reports —
# which is also the path the Daily Briefing workflow commits back to `main`, so
# leave this unset in CI.
REPORTS_DIR=
# How many days of reports are kept before the oldest are pruned. Default 30.
# The files are committed on every run, so the window is what stops the
# repository from growing without bound.
REPORTS_RETENTION_DAYS=
# The PUBLIC base URL of the dashboard, used to build the "📄 Tam rapor" links
# in the Slack message. Default if empty:
# https://beltass.github.io/AI-Executive-Assistant/
# Set it to the Vercel URL instead if that becomes the primary host.
DASHBOARD_BASE_URL=
#
# PRIVACY: the dashboard is PUBLIC (public repo, GitHub Pages + Vercel).
# Advisors whose section can contain personal data set `private = True` in code
# (today eight of the thirteen, e.g. "İletişim & Takvim Danışmanı" and
# "Toplantı Hazırlık & Takip"). Their content is
# NEVER written to frontend/reports/ — it is delivered inline in Slack instead.
# There is no environment variable for this on purpose: privacy is not a
# setting somebody can accidentally turn off.
